[{:db/id "q-351551/field-1/f630bec5e1855426811b997331df701c9b188b2bb7b95bff2b6c48c3d629cb4c" :answer/id #uuid "6428026b-b378-5e8e-95af-fae99e6edc9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t^4+12t-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351551/field-1/2c1ba280d3aa5f85b05761b2e2f874bc5b8fd64c2167269b13eb3a8baab40a37" :answer/id #uuid "0d86341d-8326-5991-8bdc-d7da1e9de60c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t^4+12t+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351551/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "7aa6d54e-0edc-56d9-b727-a82027acffee" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351551/field-1/f630bec5e1855426811b997331df701c9b188b2bb7b95bff2b6c48c3d629cb4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-351551/field-1/f630bec5e1855426811b997331df701c9b188b2bb7b95bff2b6c48c3d629cb4c" "q-351551/field-1/2c1ba280d3aa5f85b05761b2e2f874bc5b8fd64c2167269b13eb3a8baab40a37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351551" :question/id #uuid "43159458-17f0-5c7e-9f8b-8cea2a10b3e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-351551" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=8{t}^{3}+12,$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=10$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (8{t}^{3}+12)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}+12t+C \\\\  & =2{t}^{4}+12t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(1)=10.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =2(1)^{4}+12(1)+C \\\\ 10 & =2+12+C \\\\ C & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=2{t}^{4}+12t-4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351551/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351551"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351556/field-1/e58029b3faeb7bcd8c2aedfd16cba877d60aa0e97a209e7d433bc10458ce9d24" :answer/id #uuid "ae61e0c7-5705-5152-8571-c717d9390da3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\ln(t)+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351556/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "fa4068a7-9b51-5d66-bfa4-b1a30e2e8a3b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351556/field-1/e58029b3faeb7bcd8c2aedfd16cba877d60aa0e97a209e7d433bc10458ce9d24" :answer-field/choices ["q-351556/field-1/e58029b3faeb7bcd8c2aedfd16cba877d60aa0e97a209e7d433bc10458ce9d24"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351556" :question/id #uuid "d2a9c65c-7e62-5190-8aae-70c24cf9e9ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-351556" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=\\frac{6}{t},$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=4$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{6}{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(1)=4.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+C \\\\ 4 & =6(0)+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t)+4.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-351556/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351556"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7287/selection/73c9f7b185600c614e9585635e805380992cda1d9d25ff13fa8c2b8cf782956f" :answer/id #uuid "34be67e1-f61d-5387-89fc-fc3a2aee1020" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7287/selection/bb40f9ea3e9ac09e45ea07ce728519d677be35d2618693f53a4be10b4017d23a" :answer/id #uuid "b05cb132-a872-500c-9bfe-23d8c784684f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7287/selection/2cd635ead860c4313d5e00dd7bee857fb3a1eade9eb210ef30b6084ceb5d7fa4" :answer/id #uuid "18cbe422-2f6d-5d2f-955c-822d7df72b67" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{5}{36}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7287/selection/8f8af8acbfbb3d8d0e6b1573024dbbe8846c5bdae17ff0d0a7b6a3b9548479aa" :answer/id #uuid "6d25c8e8-803a-59af-998b-96ccee3a4845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7287/selection/757429a93eb8e6ba9b1c9948ecde46421854ef45247481a78d7ff00df0e2dceb" :answer/id #uuid "48eb4c88-b244-56b0-9f5e-be7bdced7153" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{2}t-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7287/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "89141635-8ccc-5802-bea9-28a3da0778d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7287/selection/8f8af8acbfbb3d8d0e6b1573024dbbe8846c5bdae17ff0d0a7b6a3b9548479aa" :answer-field/choices ["q-7287/selection/73c9f7b185600c614e9585635e805380992cda1d9d25ff13fa8c2b8cf782956f" "q-7287/selection/bb40f9ea3e9ac09e45ea07ce728519d677be35d2618693f53a4be10b4017d23a" "q-7287/selection/2cd635ead860c4313d5e00dd7bee857fb3a1eade9eb210ef30b6084ceb5d7fa4" "q-7287/selection/8f8af8acbfbb3d8d0e6b1573024dbbe8846c5bdae17ff0d0a7b6a3b9548479aa" "q-7287/selection/757429a93eb8e6ba9b1c9948ecde46421854ef45247481a78d7ff00df0e2dceb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7287" :question/id #uuid "403c8296-c4b9-5d24-b8e9-75589a7c953f" :question/math-academy-id "q-7287" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=\\frac{{t}^{2}-t}{4},$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=-\\frac{1}{6}$ when $t=2,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{{t}^{2}-t}{4})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(2)=-\\frac{1}{6}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{6} & =\\frac{1}{12}(2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}(2)^{2}+C \\\\ -\\frac{1}{6} & =\\frac{1}{6}+C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{12}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7287/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7287"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-4783/selection/a0354fb88cdc1e907a0567b4af6c4a794ba9d730c8f61700b0ee78742f13db40" :answer/id #uuid "67e73466-9782-50c3-adee-991c86822324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{3}-2t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4783/selection/66f41492dd76d612915015dfa562110703e41da74ebbb9910448d8374f259d9b" :answer/id #uuid "01afd4f7-0304-5fb9-ab11-ced9694d65e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{3}-2t+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4783/selection/b0a1b6697ddbe329590f97dba12032bc809d1b3ba9ebcebee7118d6c3b75fa47" :answer/id #uuid "bcf1191c-72b0-52d7-b8e3-9358d8f0fb33" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-2t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4783/selection/b1a5adbfb5efa653219477bfe19672ed87c68b0b16e48663e5c4ce589d5df7df" :answer/id #uuid "a043f084-3597-50f1-9033-461bb82f56d5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=3{t}^{2}-t-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4783/selection/3f8ac14ed7439679e6c84042c931ad87cd6fde56ece1f78db28ff94fab9a35b9" :answer/id #uuid "6c1032a6-da52-52d5-9b4d-1622df16969b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{3}-t+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-4783/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d9836608-64ac-5f2c-9e5e-1d9f207f3905" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-4783/selection/a0354fb88cdc1e907a0567b4af6c4a794ba9d730c8f61700b0ee78742f13db40" :answer-field/choices ["q-4783/selection/a0354fb88cdc1e907a0567b4af6c4a794ba9d730c8f61700b0ee78742f13db40" "q-4783/selection/66f41492dd76d612915015dfa562110703e41da74ebbb9910448d8374f259d9b" "q-4783/selection/b0a1b6697ddbe329590f97dba12032bc809d1b3ba9ebcebee7118d6c3b75fa47" "q-4783/selection/b1a5adbfb5efa653219477bfe19672ed87c68b0b16e48663e5c4ce589d5df7df" "q-4783/selection/3f8ac14ed7439679e6c84042c931ad87cd6fde56ece1f78db28ff94fab9a35b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-4783" :question/id #uuid "fa2039cb-4bb3-5430-9351-2f1ef471a402" :question/math-academy-id "q-4783" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=3{t}^{2}-2,$ where $t$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=-1$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (3{t}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{3}-2t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(0)=-1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =(0)^{3}-2(0)+C \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{3}-2t-1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-4783/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4783"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351770/field-1/63aa34307f3287898a82854efc8e79a5c1a8d22ff96619977df4985d8f4187c1" :answer/id #uuid "f73bf087-b07d-5a5e-89ac-8115d1ae3f2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2t+\\frac{4}{t+2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351770/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c4b1fc2-5fe7-5d88-9fdb-9b9a0e91376e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351770/field-1/63aa34307f3287898a82854efc8e79a5c1a8d22ff96619977df4985d8f4187c1" :answer-field/choices ["q-351770/field-1/63aa34307f3287898a82854efc8e79a5c1a8d22ff96619977df4985d8f4187c1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351770" :question/id #uuid "abe8be45-2c0b-5637-9cac-f08714688de3" :question/math-academy-id "q-351770" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration \n\n$$\na(t)=\\frac{8}{(t+2)^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=0$ and velocity $v=1$ when $t=0,$ the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{8}{(t+2)^{3}}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\int (t+2)^{-3}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{(t+2)^{-2}}{-2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{(t+2)^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(0)=1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{4}{(0+2)^{2}}+C \\\\ 1 & =-\\frac{4}{4}+C \\\\ 1 & =-1+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by \n\n$$\nv(t)=-\\frac{4}{(t+2)^{2}}+2.\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (-\\frac{4}{(t+2)^{2}}+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4\\int (t+2)^{-2}\\,\\text{d}t+2\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{(t+2)^{-1}}{-1}+2t+K \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{t+2}+2t+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K,$ we use the fact that $x(0)=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\frac{4}{0+2}+0+K \\\\ 0 & =2+K \\\\ K & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{4}{t+2}+2t-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351770/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43e68991-37f0-543e-a4da-b78b395a8494"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7226"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=t-2{t}^{4}$, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=\\frac{1}{10}$ and velocity $v=\\frac{1}{10}$ when $t=1$, calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (t-2{t}^{4})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-\\frac{2}{5}{t}^{5}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $v(1)=\\frac{1}{10}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}-\\frac{2}{5}(1)^{5}+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{2}{5}+C \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-\\frac{2}{5}{t}^{5}.$ \n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-\\frac{2}{5}{t}^{5})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{15}{t}^{6}+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K$, we use the fact that $x(1)=\\frac{1}{10}.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{10} & =\\frac{1}{6}(1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{15}(1)^{6}+K \\\\ \\frac{1}{10} & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{15}+K \\\\ \\frac{1}{10} & =\\frac{1}{10}+K \\\\ K & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{6}{t}^{3}-\\frac{1}{15}{t}^{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
